.TH "EPX\-MEDIA" "1" "" "epx" "epx manual"
.SH "NAME"
epx\-media \- read, upload, link and change media assets
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.RS "4"
.nf
epx media [flags]
epx media [command]
.fi
.RE
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Reads media assets: files Emporix stores (BLOB) or links to files elsewhere (LINK). ACCESS is PUBLIC or PRIVATE; STATUS is PENDING until an upload completes, then READY or empty; BYTES is the file size as sent, and REFERENCES the items an asset belongs to (type and id). URLs are only in \fB\-o json\fR; \fBepx media download\-url\fR gives one that downloads the file.
.PP
Its reads require the media.asset_read scope. Its writes require the media.asset_manage scope.
.SH "COMMANDS"
.SS "epx media create"
Create a media asset: a link, or a file to upload.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx media create [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Creates a media asset from the JSON in \fB\-\-file\fR and prints its id. A LINK asset points to a file elsewhere, e.g. \fB{"type": "LINK", "access": "PUBLIC", "url": "https://example.com/a.pdf"}\fR. A BLOB asset is a file that Emporix stores: \fB\-\-upload\fR PATH sends the file in a multipart/form\-data form, with the JSON of \fB\-\-file\fR as its body field, e.g. \fB{"type": "BLOB", "access": "PRIVATE", "details": {"filename": "a", "mimeType": "application/pdf"}}\fR. Emporix takes a file of up to 30 MB including the form; a large file may need a longer \fB\-\-timeout\fR, e.g. \fB\-\-timeout\fR 5m, as it bounds the whole request. Without \fB\-\-upload\fR, the JSON of a BLOB asset is refused before anything is sent, as Emporix takes one only with its file. refIds assigns the asset to items, e.g. \fB[{"type": "PRODUCT", "id": "100200"}]\fR; an asset of a PRODUCT or CATEGORY must be PUBLIC. An id that exists already is a conflict (exit 5).
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends POST. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the media.asset_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON in PATH, sent byte for byte: the request body, or the body field of the form of a file to upload (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR; required).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-upload <PATH>\fR
Upload the file in PATH (up to 30 MB including the form) as the file of a BLOB asset, in a multipart/form\-data form with the JSON of \fB\-\-file\fR; a large file may need a longer \fB\-\-timeout\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.PP
\fBExamples:\fR
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx media create \-\-file link.json \-\-dry\-run
epx media create \-\-upload manual.pdf \-\-file manual.json
.fi
.RE
.SS "epx media delete"
Delete a media asset.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx media delete ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Deletes the media asset ID, and the file of a BLOB asset. An unknown ID is no error: Emporix answers as for a deleted asset.
.PP
Deletes data, which cannot be undone. On a terminal, epx sends DELETE only once you type ID at its prompt. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the media.asset_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal).
.SS "epx media download\-url"
Show a URL that downloads an asset.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx media download\-url ASSET_ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads a URL that downloads an asset. For a private stored file it is a signed URL that works without a token until EXPIRES (15 minutes by default), so treat it as a secret; for a public file or a link, PROVIDER CLOUDINARY or LINK, it is the asset\(aqs permanent URL. Reading the URL of a pending upload whose file is stored makes Emporix complete it; one whose file is not stored yet fails. ASSET_ID is the ID that \fBepx media list\fR shows; an unknown one is not found.
.PP
Requires the media.asset_read scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among PROVIDER, EXPIRES, URL.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.SS "epx media get"
Show one asset.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx media get ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads media assets: files Emporix stores (BLOB) or links to files elsewhere (LINK). ACCESS is PUBLIC or PRIVATE; STATUS is PENDING until an upload completes, then READY or empty; BYTES is the file size as sent, and REFERENCES the items an asset belongs to (type and id). URLs are only in \fB\-o json\fR; \fBepx media download\-url\fR gives one that downloads the file.
.PP
Requires the media.asset_read scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among ID, TYPE, ACCESS, STATUS, FILE, MIME TYPE, BYTES, REFERENCES.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.SS "epx media list"
List media assets.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx media list [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads media assets: files Emporix stores (BLOB) or links to files elsewhere (LINK). ACCESS is PUBLIC or PRIVATE; STATUS is PENDING until an upload completes, then READY or empty; BYTES is the file size as sent, and REFERENCES the items an asset belongs to (type and id). URLs are only in \fB\-o json\fR; \fBepx media download\-url\fR gives one that downloads the file.
.PP
Requires the media.asset_read scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among ID, TYPE, ACCESS, STATUS, FILE, MIME TYPE, BYTES, REFERENCES.
.TP
\fB\-\-limit <n>\fR
Print at most n items; paged reads stop early where they safely can (0: every item).
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-query <filter>\fR
Emporix q filter, passed as given, e.g. code:(A1,A2); space\-separated conditions must all match (fields mostly as in \fB\-o json\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-sort <order>\fR
Emporix sort order, passed as given, e.g. code or name.en:desc,code; fields mostly as in \fB\-o json\fR (Emporix may ignore an unknown one).
.TP
\fB\-\-stream\fR
Print items as JSON Lines as soon as they are checked, page by page on paged lists, reading up to 10000 pages where a list without it stops after 1000: a check failing on a later page exits 1 after the pages before it (excludes \fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-columns\fR and \fB\-\-no\-headers\fR).
.SS "epx media patch"
Change members of a media asset.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx media patch ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Changes the media asset ID with the JSON Patch (RFC 6902) in \fB\-\-file\fR, an array of operations such as \fB[{"op": "add", "path": "/refIds/\-", "value": {"type": "PRODUCT", "id": "100200"}}]\fR, also of a BLOB asset, whose file it keeps; its type and access cannot change. An unknown ID is not found (exit 4).
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends PATCH. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the media.asset_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR; required).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.SS "epx media start\-upload"
Start an upload of a file straight to storage.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx media start\-upload [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Starts an upload session: creates a PENDING BLOB asset from the JSON in \fB\-\-file\fR, as create takes it (\fB"uploadType"\fR: \fB"form"\fR asks for a form instead of a PUT for a PRIVATE asset), and prints where to send its file: the method, URL and headers or form fields of a request to the storage (GCS for a PRIVATE asset, CLOUDINARY for a PUBLIC one), valid for 15 minutes or an hour, so treat it as a secret. epx does not send the file there; once the storage has it, the asset is READY. Emporix enables direct uploads per tenant; elsewhere it answers 403 Forbidden (exit 1) and creates no asset.
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends POST. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the media.asset_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR; required).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.SS "epx media update"
Replace a media asset, or the file of one.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx media update ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Replaces the media asset ID with the JSON in \fB\-\-file\fR; its type and access cannot change. The JSON of a LINK asset gives its url; a BLOB asset is replaced with its file: \fB\-\-upload\fR PATH sends the new file in a multipart/form\-data form, with the JSON as its body field (up to 30 MB including the form; a large file may need a longer \fB\-\-timeout\fR, e.g. \fB\-\-timeout\fR 5m). \fBepx media patch\fR changes a BLOB asset without sending its file again. Without \fB\-\-upload\fR, the JSON of a BLOB asset is refused before anything is sent, as Emporix takes one only with its file. An unknown ID is not found (exit 4).
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends PUT. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the media.asset_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON in PATH, sent byte for byte: the request body, or the body field of the form of a file to upload (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR; required).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-upload <PATH>\fR
Upload the file in PATH (up to 30 MB including the form) as the file of a BLOB asset, in a multipart/form\-data form with the JSON of \fB\-\-file\fR; a large file may need a longer \fB\-\-timeout\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
